This work addresses the analysis of $a$-adic solenoids and provides solutions to the functional equation $\sum_{k=0}^{p-1} f(x+\omega_p)=\Phi(x)$ and $\sum_{
u=0}^{\infty} a^{-
u\gamma}f(a^{
u+1}x+a^{ 
u}b)=\Phi(x)$ on these structures. We extend the $\Phi$-functions to be well-defined and bounded on $a$-adic solenoids and demonstrate their applicability to the $p$-adic analog of the generalized Polya theorem and a $p$-adic version of Whittaker-Shattnov interpolation formula.
